+## Symlinks
+
+Symbolic links stored in an archive are skipped unless the
+`-l/--links` flag is in use. With `-l/--links` they are exposed as
+regular files with a `.rclonelink` extension whose contents are the
+link target, so `rclone copy --links :archive:archive.zip /tmp/out`
+recreates them as symlinks at a destination which supports them.
+
+Zip files only store symlinks when created with `zip -y`; squashfs
+images store them natively.
+
